<http://data.silknow.org/object/bd6955fa-6669-3398-bf2b-dd5f32560c64>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Shawl of brocaded wool and silk, Great Britain, 1840-1845"@en , "Shawl of brocaded wool and silk. The white ground is made of a twill weave with a wool warp on silk weft, and covered with jewel-like widely spaced repeated motifs woven in bright vermilion, mid-green, mid-blue, yellow and black, all with jagged edges of 'shawl pattern'. The pattern is brocaded with two shoots of woollen weft together, bound in tabby by a portion of the warp. \n\nRow one of the pattern consists of a foliate-pointed oval shape, green in one row, blue in the next, with small red flowers and berries springing from it, and within it a red flower-head in a lozenge. Row two of the pattern consists of small sprays of fantastic flowers curving alternately to left and right in the same row, and staggered from row one.\n\nThe shawl has an applied fringe of white silk, knotted into tassels, round all four sides."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/35b4f3a8-0a50-31ba-9e30-9720656806ec> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/ff534bfb-215f-360a-8b33-7486d801bd59> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/cac2e132-4cad-3fa3-a0e0-c68a0cc164c6> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Shawl of brocaded wool and silk. The white ground is made of a twill weave with a wool warp on silk weft, and covered with jewel-like widely spaced repeated motifs woven in bright vermilion, mid-green, mid-blue, yellow and black, all with jagged edges of 'shawl pattern'. The pattern is brocaded with two shoots of woollen weft together, bound in tabby by a portion of the warp. \n\nRow one of the pattern consists of a foliate-pointed oval shape, green in one row, blue in the next, with small red flowers and berries springing from it, and within it a red flower-head in a lozenge. Row two of the pattern consists of small sprays of fantastic flowers curving alternately to left and right in the same row, and staggered from row one.\n\nThe shawl has an applied fringe of white silk, knotted into tassels, round all four sides."@en , "Shawl of brocaded wool and silk, Great Britain, 1840-1845"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/bd6955fa-6669-3398-bf2b-dd5f32560c64/dimension/3> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/bd6955fa-6669-3398-bf2b-dd5f32560c64/dimension/4> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/bd6955fa-6669-3398-bf2b-dd5f32560c64/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/bd6955fa-6669-3398-bf2b-dd5f32560c64/dimension/2> ;
